keepass-auto-merge (0.3.2) unstable; urgency=low

  * Fix: the service unit used LoadCredential=, which searches only the plain
    credential store. The credential lives in /etc/credstore.encrypted/, so
    systemd silently started the service without the password and the run
    failed with "credential not found". The unit now uses
    LoadCredentialEncrypted=, which decrypts the credential at start.

 -- willthong <willthong@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 13 Nov 2026 16:25:00 +0000

keepass-auto-merge (0.3.1) unstable; urgency=low

  * Fix: verify/run outside systemd must be run as root because systemd's
    credential host key is root-only. The error now says so, and the README
    shows `sudo keepass-auto-merge verify` instead of a bare call that fails
    with "Permission denied".

 -- willthong <willthong@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 13 Nov 2026 15:20:00 +0000

keepass-auto-merge (0.3.0) unstable; urgency=low

  * Fix: verify and run decrypt the stored credential when they are not
    running under systemd. Previously the ciphertext was fed to the merge
    engine, which looked exactly like a wrong password.
  * Fix: engine failures now include keepassxc-cli's own diagnosis.
  * Remove the merge_mode setting: the merge is always keep-newer.
  * Remove the keepassxc_cli setting: there is no alternative engine.

 -- willthong <willthong@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 13 Nov 2026 15:05:00 +0000

keepass-auto-merge (0.2.1) unstable; urgency=low

  * Fix: removing or upgrading the package no longer fails or complains when a
    unit it expects was never installed.
  * README: install with `apt install ./<file>.deb`, because `dpkg -i` does not
    resolve the package's dependencies.

 -- willthong <willthong@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 13 Nov 2026 14:40:00 +0000

keepass-auto-merge (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=low

  * configure: write the configuration file from flags or interactive prompts,
    regenerate the units for the watch directory, and apply them.
  * Every verb refuses an unconfigured install and says what to run.
  * The packaged conffile is defaults-only, comment-free, and readable by the
    service user; comments in the config are no longer preserved.
  * Fix: the package now depends on python3-tomli-w.

 -- willthong <willthong@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 13 Nov 2026 12:15:00 +0000

